## Setting Comparison at a Glance

| Setting | Corner Protection | Adds Visual Size | Best For | Setting Price Range |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Solitaire 4-prong | Low | No | Maximum stone visibility | $990–$1,400 |
| Bezel | High | Slightly reduces | Active lifestyle, modern look | $990–$4,500 |
| Cathedral | Low-Med | Slightly | Elevated traditional look | $1,240–$2,890 |
| Cathedral Pavé | Low-Med | Slightly | Band sparkle on a budget | $1,800–$2,890 |
| Marquise Side Stone | Low | Yes (width) | Wider ring appearance | $1,250–$1,970 |
| Baguette Side Stone | Low | Yes (length) | Art Deco, statement rings | $4,190–$4,625 |
| Halo | Low | High (~25%) | Maximum visual size | $2,470–$4,550 |
| Hidden Halo | Low | Minimal | Subtle sparkle boost | $1,255–$1,970 |

**Verdict:** No single setting is best for everyone. Solitaire if you want the stone front and center. Bezel if you worry about damage. Cathedral pavé if you want band sparkle without a halo. Halo if visual size is the priority.

